# CODEOWNERS — who must approve changes to which paths (build-hardening-kit).
# With branch protection's "require review from Code Owners", nothing merges
# into an owned path without an owner's approval. Last match wins.
[% if code_owners %]
*                          [[ code_owners ]]

# Recorded debt: growing it needs an owner's approval, which GitHub records.
eslint-suppressions.json   [[ code_owners ]]
.gitleaksignore            [[ code_owners ]]
.copier-answers.yml        [[ code_owners ]]
.github/                   [[ code_owners ]]
[% else %]
#
# EDIT BEFORE RELYING ON IT. GitHub silently ignores owners that do not exist,
# so a placeholder owner makes "require review from Code Owners" enforce
# nothing. Uncomment and set real users or teams (or re-run
# `copier update --trust --data code_owners=@your-org/your-team`).
#
# *                          @your-org/maintainers
# eslint-suppressions.json   @your-org/maintainers
# .gitleaksignore            @your-org/maintainers
# .github/                   @your-org/maintainers
[% endif %]
